    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear directive: capitalize on favorable platoon matchups and exploit the base-stealing potential against soft-delivering arms. Our top play today is **Trea Turner** (81.27), who benefits from a prime matchup against a lefty in a favorable park, paired with **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42), whose dynamic platoon edge against the same arm makes him a must-start. However, the highest ceiling belongs to **Christian Yelich** (75.84). With the lineup pending, **Christian Yelich** earns an elite grade by projecting into the leadoff spot against a hittable righty; his ability to pair a 14% park boost with a 13% SP skill advantage\u2014and the added boost from the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014makes him a cornerstone for our stolen base pursuit. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (66.86) also remains a core start, as the wind-out conditions and SP matchup outweigh his negative platoon differential.\n\nOur roster depth forced a difficult cut at the utility spot, where **Chase Meidroth** (44.60) narrowly missed the final lineup. While **Chase Meidroth** offers reliable base metrics and an order advantage, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace **Junior Caminero** (52.96). Despite **Junior Caminero** facing a tough matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA starter, his raw talent profile maintains a higher floor than **Chase Meidroth**, who was ultimately benched to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Gary Sanchez**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Carson Benge**, and **Junior Caminero** while waiting for confirmed lineups. If any of these names are pushed down the order\u2014particularly **Carson Benge**\u2014we may see their scores drift toward the marginal range. We are also continuing to monitor the development of **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** in the minors, alongside the inactive **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom are ready to be integrated should our current starters falter or succumb to injury.",
